id: pm-dhlij3
title: "An installed extension whose registerItemFields names a reserved item key makes every pm create and pm update fail with untyped command_failed, and package doctor does not name the cause"
description: "Measured 2026-11-23 on the 2026.11.23 build while closing pm-3s4jwl. A project extension that calls api.registerItemFields([{ name: 'priority', type: 'string' }]) activates without a refusal. Afterwards every pm create (with or without --field) and every pm update (pm update <id> --title t2) exits 2 with code command_failed and the detail 'Extension item field \"priority\" collides with built-in item metadata \"priority\"; rename the extension field...'. Reads keep working (pm list returns items). pm package doctor reports only extension_custom_field_mcp_input_collision for the field, and pm health --check-only says nothing about it, so the operator sees a tracker whose writes all fail with an untyped code and no diagnostic that names the package. pm-ghf1 (closed) added the reserved-key check to SDK lint, preflight and the test harness, so a package author is warned, but an already published or hand-written package still disables all writes for every user of the tracker. Duplicate check: searched 'extension item field collides with built-in item metadata reserved create fails'; pm-ghf1 owns authoring-time detection only, pm-3s4jwl owns built-in option collisions."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:sdk",extensions,schema,ux
created_at: "2026-11-23T08:45:02.256Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-27T04:03:26.215Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-27T04:03:25.551Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-27T04:03:25.551Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Activation refuses only the reserved field registration with a typed code that names the package, the field and the reserved key, and pm create and pm update keep working for every other field; pm package doctor and pm health report the refused registration with the package name and a rename hint; A regression spec installs such an extension and drives create and update on the built CLI, with a negative control showing the pre-fix refusal"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "registerItemFields drops only a field named after built-in item metadata and emits extension_item_field_reserved:<layer>:<package>:<field>:rename=<prefix>_<field>, which package doctor and health report; the create and update write paths share applyRegisteredItemFieldDefaultsForWrite, which keeps typed refusal codes instead of rebuilding them as command_failed"
expected_result: One package's reserved field name cannot disable writes for the whole tracker; the refusal is typed and diagnosable
actual_result: "On the built CLI with such a package installed, create --field review_owner=ada and update --title exit 0, and doctor and health list the warning naming the package, field and rename; a hand-built registry that still reaches the write path is refused with extension_item_field_reserved instead of command_failed"
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-3s4jwl,discovered_from,"2026-11-23T08:45:02.256Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
  pm-ghf1,related,"2026-11-23T08:45:02.256Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-27T03:31:48.250Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause and fix (2026-11-27, branch fix/field-admission-diagnostics). Two defects combined: (1) the loader accepted a registerItemFields definition named after built-in item metadata, and every write then ran applyRegisteredItemFieldDefaultsAndValidation, which refuses the reserved name; (2) create.ts and update.ts wrapped that call in a catch that rebuilt every error as a plain PmCliError, so the typed extension_item_field_reserved code (and extension_item_field_type_conflict) surfaced as command_failed. Fix: ExtensionApiRegistrar.registerItemFields drops only the reserved field and pushes the activation warning extension_item_field_reserved:<layer>:<package>:<field>:rename=<prefix>_<field> (formatReservedItemFieldWarning in src/core/extensions/item-fields.ts); a registration that held only reserved fields registers nothing. Both write paths now call applyRegisteredItemFieldDefaultsForWrite, which rethrows a PmCliError unchanged and turns the validation TypeErrors into usage refusals. Activation warnings already reach package doctor and health, so both now name the package, field and rename; the MCP input collision row for the dropped field disappears with it. Evidence on the built CLI in a sandbox tracker: create --field review_owner=ada exits 0, update --title exits 0, doctor and health list the warning; tests/unit/extensions/extension-item-field-admission.spec.ts (5 cases) covers activation, the write path (a hand-built registry is the negative control that still reaches the write path), and the built CLI. Negative control: with src reverted to main, all 5 cases fail."
  "2026-11-27T04:02:40.566Z","harness:claude-code","Correction to the fix note above (2026-11-27): a registerItemFields call whose fields are all reserved now keeps an empty registration entry instead of registering nothing. The package did register against the schema capability, so the harness least-privilege check (assertExtensionCapabilityUsage) and capability usage stay truthful; registration_counts.item_fields counts fields, so it still reports 0 for that call. Test fixtures in sdk-index.spec.ts and extension-loader.spec.ts that asserted registered fields named severity and risk (both reserved item keys, so those fields already broke every write) now use incident_severity and risk_score. The write-path helper is imported directly from core/extensions/item-fields.js so it does not join the public ./sdk surface."
files[6]{path,scope,note}:
  src/core/extensions/item-fields.ts,project,formatReservedItemFieldWarning; applyRegisteredItemFieldDefaultsForWrite keeps typed refusals
  src/core/extensions/loader.ts,project,registerItemFields drops a reserved field with an activation warning
